        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-16T03:21:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I mixed cc/tidy.go and cc/config/tidy.go.\nI would like to minimize builder.go\u0027s dependency on both of them.\n\nIn fact, some code in cc/config/tidy.go, such as TidyReduceCFlags,\nshould be moved into cc/tidy.go, so that cc/config/tidy.go will be\nmore like other config/*.go files. It should only define host/device/target/clang-version dependent variables and some interface functions.\ncc/tidy.go should have config-independent logic\nand have minimal dependency on cc/config/tidy.go.",
      "parentUuid": "2c47e876_30fa8ef2",
      "revId": "42e2323e1d89e19a9245a19cd81b823a5dbac894",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f61b46b_c5ff375b",
        "filename": "cc/builder.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 444,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-19T19:45:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I prefer the current layering.  tidy.go handles the module-level flag processing.  builder.go converts the flags struct to rules.  The shareFlags code makes sense there, because it is also handling the non-tidy rules.  builder.go gets config-type data from config/tidy.go, which localizes the data stored in code.\n\nYou could move TidyReduceCFlags into tidy.go, but I don\u0027t think it has much value, it\u0027s a tiny wrapper around the regex in config/tidy.go.\n\nI like your refactorings though, but they should stay in builder.go.",
      "parentUuid": "c59c9d01_829599bc",
      "revId": "42e2323e1d89e19a9245a19cd81b823a5dbac894",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
